                "Over the past five years, the global social media ecosystem underwent a profound structural transformation: the decisive transition from the Social Graph to the Algorithmic Interest Graph. In the legacy era of social media (dominated by early Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram), distribution was governed by the social graph: users explicitly followed friends, family, and brands, and content was distributed chronologically or semi-chronologically to that established follower base. Building a social media brand meant accumulating a massive follower count—a vanity metric that corporate boards celebrated as a proprietary marketing distribution asset.",
